WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.630
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:05.910
With big data, we've come to
expect big responsibility.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.550
In order to handle the
complexity of today's data,

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.510
you need to spend
a lot on hardware,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.980
plan ahead for
scalability, and pour hours

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.472
into system architecture.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:16.420
It's no joke.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.100
And this just gets
you up and running.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.940
You still need someone-- no, a
team to make sure everything's

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.730
running smoothly.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.320
And even after
all that headache,

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.800
running queries can still take
anywhere from minutes to hours,

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.980
and mistakes can be costly.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.980
Wouldn't you rather focus on
finding insights from your data

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.275
than developing the
infrastructure around it?

00:00:39.945 --> 00:00:42.595
Google BigQuery is a fully
managed data warehouse

00:00:42.595 --> 00:00:48.570
that removes set up hassles and
runs queries rocket fast, fast

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.270
enough to analyze
terabytes of the data

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.056
in seconds,
petabytes in minutes.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.290
Google BigQuery works on
a pay-as-you-go basis.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.330
You only pay for
the bytes processed.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.360
What if you have a
really big query?

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.811
It's simple.

00:01:03.811 --> 00:01:05.269
We'll spin up an
entire data center

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:07.120
to quickly process it for you.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.280
Just sit back, and let
us handle the scaling.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.420
Google BigQuery
encrypts, replicates,

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.560
and deploys your data
across multiple data

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.190
centers for maximum durability
and service up time.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.117
With just a couple
of clicks, you

00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:22.466
can control where
you store your data.

00:01:22.466 --> 00:01:25.290
Sharing and collaboration
are easy as well.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:28.160
You decide who can
access your data.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.610
And because you can use
standard SQL queries,

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.460
anyone can get involved.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.490
Plus, BigQuery integrates
with Google Cloud Platform

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.480
products and other
software, so you can readily

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.200
load, process, and make
interactive visualizations

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.410
of your data.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:46.380
It's never been easier to
analyze massive data sets

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.906
and find insights fast
with Google BigQuery.

00:01:48.906 --> 00:01:51.350
Head to
cloud.google.com/bigquery.

